Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 AUG 98 at 09 41 CLINICAL DATA   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  tumor  status post chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  3 CM  EXTENDING FOCALLY TO THE ANTERIOR INFERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  WITH FOCI OF LYMPHATIC INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  CONFINED TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  Note  No vascular invasion is seen  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR INFERIOR MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  Note  Two lymph nodes show extension of metastatic carcinoma outside the lymph node capsule  In one of these lymph nodes  the extension into perinodal adipose tissue is marked  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  07 AUG 98 at 19 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 23     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAS  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a 6 x 5 x 4cm portion of breast tissue with an attached 3 x 2 x 0 9cm ellipse of skin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 3 x 2 x 1 2cm fibrous area with focal yellow necrosis that grossly extends to the anterior inferior resection margins  Frozen sections are performed on representative sections from the tumor with the anterior inferior margin  as FX 1 and FX 2  The remaining specimen is adipose with few white  firm branching areas  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  FX 1 and FX 2  respectively  C  Mass  D  Mass with deep margin  E  Mass with anterior inferior margin  F  Firm area close to the deep margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral margin  short stitch superior  long stitch new lateral margin  is a 4 x 2 x 1 5cm portion of breast tissue oriented by a long and short suture  The specimen is grossly unremarkable  The new lateral margin is inked in black  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  G  Lower half of the specimen  H  Upper half of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional anterior inferior margin  long stitch lateral  short new inferior  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 8cm portion of adipose breast tissue oriented by a long and a short suture  The specimen is grossly unremarkable  The new inferior margin is inked in black and the specimen is entirely submitted as follows  I J  Lateral half of the specimen  K  Medial half of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  are multiple  irregular portions of breast tissue varying from 1cm to 3cm and aggregating to 5 x 3 x 1 5cm  The specimens are grossly unremarkable  They are sectioned and entirely submitted in five cassettes L through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a 5 x 4 x 4cm portion of adipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes  The larges is 2cm with an adipose cut surface  The lymph nodes are submitted in four cassettes Q through T  Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 AND  2  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH INFILTRATING CARCINOMA LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE MM OF THE CLOSEST  AND INKED  RESECTION MARGIN IN FX  1  TUMOR IS WITHIN CAUTERIZED TISSUE  TUMOR IN FX 2 IS NOT AS CLOSE TO THE MARGIN  SPECIMEN TAKEN INTO O R  TO SHOW SURGEON WH