Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 07 CLINICAL DATA  Spiculated lesion on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL FOCI THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma combines features of both ductal and lobular carcinomas and therefore poses problems of classification  I favor the diagnosis of infiltrating lobular carcinoma  but others would choose the diagnosis of infiltrating ductal carcinoma  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion are not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm soft yellow red piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing needle in place and accompanying x ray  A 1 0cm firm area is located in the center of this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm stellate  hard  gritty white lesion coming to within 0 1cm of the inked margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow and soft  A representative section of the gritty lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen  the remaining sections of the lesion submitted in A through E  uninvolved breast in F through K  entirely  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  , Unchecked.
