Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 23 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SPECIMEN  1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA GRADE 1 SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT   SPECIMEN  2  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  TWO SEPARATE FOCI SPANNING REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  ONE FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MEDIAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASSES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   Specimens  1 and  2  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate parts  Labeled  left breast  1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm gritty white nodule  abutting inked resection margin  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The rest of the tumor is submitted in A C  The remainder of the breast biopsy entirely in DandE  Labeled  left breast  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm oriented breast biopsy  A small suture with a single knot designates the deep superior margin  the area abutting the specimen  1  This area is inked blue over black  A suture with two knots designates the lateral margin of the specimen  and is now inked green  The superficial resection margin is inked red  The medial resection margin is inked yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 7cm in greatest diameter stellate white firm nodule  within  0 1cm of the superficial  red ink  resection margin  The second nodule is more laterally located  and is 1 4cm in greatest dimension  firm  grossly abutting the anterior resection margin of the specimen  Submitted entirely from medial to lateral in F N with medial  small  nodule entirely in G I  and the larger  lateral  nodule entirely in J H  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                        