ive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two separately labeled parts  Labeled  left breast  stitch on top of axillary contents   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  11 x REMOVED_DATE x 4cm  with an attached 13 x 5 5cm skin ellipse  and 9 x 2 x 1 5cm axillary tail  The skins contains a 2 2cm curved scar located 1cm superolateral to the nipple  Specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm irregular cavity located 0 4cm deep to the scar and extending to within 1cm of the nearest deep margin  Cavity is filled with red brown hemorrhage and surrounded by focally gritty tan yellow tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma is rubbery  tan white  and contains numerous cysts ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in diameter  The axillary tail contains several  approximately 6  soft red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm in diameter  SECTION CODE  A  biopsy cavity including nearest deep margin B D  representative biopsy cavity E G  representative breast parenchyma H  representative nipple IandJ  lymph nodes from axillary tail  Labeled  highest left axillary nodes  stitch on highest   is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing multiple  approximately 7   soft tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in grea