ATE x 0 7cm portion of yellow breast tissue with a stitch designating the surface furthest from the tumor  The stitched surface is inked black and the opposite surface is inked blue  Specimen is serially sectioned  revealing unremarkable tan white to yellow breast tissue  The entire specimen has been submitted in cassettes L N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of yellow breast tissue with a stitch on one surface designated as furthest from tumor  The stitched surface is inked black and the opposite surface is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned  revealing unremarkable yellow and tan white breast tissue  The entirely specimen is submitted in cassettes O P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node   are three fragments of yellow brown fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm in aggregate  Within the specimen are multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm  All the lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes Q W  with Q R containing whole lymph nodes and S W each containing one lymph node  bisected  Resident  VINCENT KO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART D  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY   EXCISION , Checked.
