ons of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate specimens   Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm unoriented breast excision specimen  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan  firm  somewhat well defined mass  extending to less than 1mm from an inked resection margin  Representative sections in A D  Next to the periphery of the lesion is a tan  soft  ill defined area which extends to the inked margin  representative section in E   Right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary lymph node dissection containing multiple nodules  REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest diameter  representative sections in F J  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLA  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
