Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Kristina Braaten  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Needle localization lumpectomy for right breast mass  Status post chemotherapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CALCIFICATIONS ASSOCIATED WITH THE TUMOR AND WITH BENIGN LOBULES   SEE TABLE AND NOTE   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  GRADE  Not applicable  post chemotherapy specimen   LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Suspicious  see note   BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to   0 1cm from the inferior and inferior lateral margin of the specimen in multiple foci  and is focally 0 2cm from the superior margin of the specimen  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of the mass  MARGINS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Significant invasive tumor is present throughout the 2 4cm region  associated with fibrosis  There is significant  cleft artifact  around the infiltrating tumor  making assessment of lymphatic invasion difficult  A few foci are suspicious  Additional studies are in progress to further assess this aspect  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR MARGIN  UNORIENTED   EXCISION  FOCAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  ASSOCIATED WITH MINUTE FOCUS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INVOLVING 2 OF 4 BLOCKS  SPANNING UP TO REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE FINAL MARGIN  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The inferior margin is inked black  the superior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm indurated gray white poorly delineated region which abuts the inferior margin and comes to 0 4cm of the superior  0 4cm of the anterior  0 6cm of the lateral  1 0cm of the medial  and 1 1cm of the anterior margin  A silver metal clip is noted along the anterior aspect of the area  and the area is between the two localization wires  The remaining mammary tissue is dense gray white and fibrous  Representative sections are submitted from posterior to anterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the tissue bearing the silver metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the firm area as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  posterior right margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unoriented tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  The unoriented specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  There is a suture along one aspect designating the new margin  The new sutured margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan yellow lobulated portion of lymph node bearing fatty tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in maximum dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node  Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for vascular markers   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   are difficult to interpret  but are somewhat helpful in excluding extensive lymphatic invasion  However  the findings on routine stains remain focally suspicious for lymphatic invasion  Addendum  3 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT POSTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL LATERALMARGIN   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  WITH FOCAL SPINDLE CELL METAPLASIA  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODE  INTRAMAMMARY   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm overlying skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The superior border of the skin ellipse is marked with a stitch  A 1 0cm in diameter  brown plaque is located at 6 0cm lateral and superior to the nipple  overlying a firm mass below the skin  The resection margins are inked black  the anterior superior resection surface is double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE tan to white  firm mass located beneath the skin lesion that extends to within 0 2cm of the posterior resection margin  The mass has a 1 0cm diameter irregular shaped cystic cavity containing white mucoid fluids  A 2 0cm in diameter white nodular mass is located at 5 0cm lateral to the first lesion  and appears well circumscribed  extends to within 0 2cm from the posterior resection margin  The second mass is located directly beneath the lateral end of the skin ellipse  at the base of the axillary tail  Section code  A  first mass at its closest resection margin  deep  B  first mass at skin C and D  sections taken from the medial and the lateral portion of the first mass  respectively E  second mass at its nearest resection margin  deep  F  the medial most section of the second mass G  the lateral most section of the second mass H L  nodes from axillary tail Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 13 CLINICAL DATA  Forty seven year old with incidentally found left breast nodule  Biopsy showed extensive ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  AND ADDITIONAL AXILLARY CONTENTS  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING  40   AND INTRADUCTAL  60   CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The examined inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  Lymphatic invasion is not seen  Carcinoma is present in five of six slides of breast  Nipple is unremarkable  Fourteen of fourteen axillary lymph nodes are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 29     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     The residual tumor size is greater than 2cm in overall extent  Because of the multifocal nature of the carcinoma  a more accurate size cannot be expressed  No gross lesion was present  Added by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast  is a 22 x 18 x 4 8cm left breast with an attached 7 x 6 x 1 5cm portion of axillary tissue  The contained skin with unremarkable nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  with a 6cm in length well healed scar along the superior margin  Two sutures are in place  a long suture laterally and a short suture superiorly  The axillary tissue contains multiple firm and enlarged lymph nodes  tan red on cut section and measuring up to 2 1cm in length  The breast parenchyma contains multiple confluent areas of linear tan gray firm tissue streaks  the largest confluent area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  This confluent area contains cystic spaces filled with soft  yellow tan material  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of more red colored fibrous tissue  located medially and just beneath the medial border of the skin scar  No discrete biopsy cavity is noted  No discrete nodules are noted  The area of red colored fibrous tissue extends to within 2 5cm of the nearest margin  which is deep  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a 2 5cm in diameter aggregate of fibroadipose tissue which contains two fragmented lymph nodes  tan pink in color and measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in length  Section Code A   lymph nodes   additional axillary   2 B E   axillary tail lymph nodes  main specimen F   nipple and skin scar G H   red colored fibrous tissue  possible previous biopsy site I J   fibrous tissue with cystic areas containing soft tan material K M   representative breast tissue Resident  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  POSITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE PART B  LEFT BREAST and AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 18 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING MULTIFOCALLY TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is 1cm in greatest dimension  No unequivocal lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Estrogen receptor studies will be performed on formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tissue and will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   with attached specimen x ray   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing no gross lesion large enough to freeze  A 0 7cm ill  defined  slightly firm and gritty area is present at an inked margin  The nodule is submitted entirely in A through C  the remainder of the tissue in D through N  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
