cm tan skin ellipse with underlying fibrous and adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  There is a superficial scar on the skin at approximately 1 o clock  that is 2 2cm long and is 3 5cm from the nipple  There is a stitch to orient the specimen  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  The biopsy cavity is round  soft  tan red yellow and heterogenous  It is well defined and is rimmed by white yellow tissue  This biopsy cavity comes to within 1 4cm to the deep margin  Adjacent to the biopsy site is an area of hemorrhage and blue dye  This area is lateral and inferior to the biopsy site  In these areas  is noted soft yellow material that can be extruded from areas with pressure  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A F  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity  Please note cassettes A and B contain biopsy cavity and its relation to the nearest margin  G J  Representative sections of the adjacent areas with the yellow punctate soft material  K L  Representative sections of breast tissue away from the lesion  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lymph node  The specimen is bivalved and frozen in toto as FX diagnosis  1  now resubmitted in cassette M  Resident  JOSHUA B  KISH  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  JULIA TURBINER  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  GREGORY LAUWERS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTIN