erone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy left axillary node dissection   is a 21 x 7 x 2 4cm lumpectomy specimen with attached axilla  There are three guide wires in the specimen and a long stitch marking the lateral and axillary lateral margin and axillary tail  short stitch demarcating the anterior margin  and a bow tie demarcating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal tan yellow adipose tissue with intermixed white fibrous tissue  and numerous palpable nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The nodules are ill defined and in most cases not visually discrete from the surrounding adipose and fibrous tissue  However the largest mentioned nodule is tan pink to tan white and is adjacent to a curled surgical clip  This largest nodule is 0 5cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin 2 5cm from the inferior margin  2 2cm from the superior margin  and greater than 3 0cm from both the medial and lateral margins  The surgical clip is removed and representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Dominant nodule to anterior margin adjacent to curled clip  B C  Additional sections of nodule to anterior margin  D  Nodule to post