strogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a mastectomy specimen REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm and 900 grams  designated with a short stitch for superior aspect and a long stitch for lateral aspect  with a REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm retracted nipple  A 5 5cm well healed surgical scar is present 1 5cm superior to the nipple  Attached to the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan to pink focally yellow firm mass under the nipple and 1 8cm from the closest  deep  inked resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is mostly fatty with some fibrous area medial to the main mass  SECTION CODE  A E  representative sections of tumor F  nipple with underlying tumor G  nearest deep resection margin  radial section H  fibrous area with nearest deep resection margin I J  and K  axillary lymph nodes  Also received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5