Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  90   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  10     SEE NOTE   2  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMATOSIS  NOTE  The invasive component extends to an inked resectin margin and measures 0 6cm from the glass slide  No definit lymphatic or vasular invasion is noted  The in situ component has some micropapillary features  Diagnosis by  XXSOUTHERN JAMES F  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 04 Proofread by  XXSOUTHERN JAMES F                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 05     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of cauterized  semifirm breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma with multiple cysts measuring up to 0 3cm in diameter  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes A and B  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIANGOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FLIEDER DOUGLAS  NO ADDRESS  O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS , Unchecked.
