Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  John H Eichhorn  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Tissue Processed CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma  with positive margins on prior excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING NUMEROUS CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE OR IN SITU CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  long  lateral  short  superior   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm portion of tan red fibrofatty breast tissue with a short black stitch designating the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  An exposed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with a previous biopsy site is along the anterior aspect  The cavity has been previously and partially stitched together with black sutures  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a focal bright yellow area consistent with fat necrosis surrounding the hemorrhagic cavity  The cavity focally abuts the medial margin  and comes to 0 9cm of the lateral  1 4cm of the posterior  0 5cm of the inferior  and 2 2cm of the superior margin  The surrounding focally dense gray white fibrous tissue shows cystic change  The clear serous fluid filled cysts average 0 2cm in diameter  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm gray yellow calcification within the dense gray white fibrous tissue  0 9cm from the cavity and 1 4cm from the closest posterior margin in the mid to inferior portion of the specimen  Another cluster of gritty tan yellow calcifications measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and is located inferior to the first  0 4cm from the closest medial margin  and 1 7cm from the cavity  The remaining fibrous tissue shows focal nodularity with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the cavity to closest margins as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The first calcified focus is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the second as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections along the posterior and posteromedial aspect of the cavity  the region corresponding to the margin of concern in the prior excision  are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  This case was reviewed again  and at the request of the patient  who is a physician  additional tissue from the specimen was submitted for processing in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A single duct in profile within the biopsy cavity wall on one of the eight additional slides shows residual ductal carcinoma in situ  and this tiny focus is 1 0cm from a blue inked margin  anterior   No stromal or lymphatic invasion is identified in the additional sections  Fibrocystic changes  harboring calcifications  are again noted  Addendum  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT  RE  EXCISION , Unchecked.
