s antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Medial breast margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm tan gray tissue fragment  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  1  now A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast tumor and block with left axillary nodes  level 1 and level 2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm specimen consisting of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm fragment of breast with attached axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm skin ellipse overlying the breast  1 5cm deep to the skin is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm well circumscribed  gray white  glistening nodule with a cut gritty surface  This mass is 0 6cm closest to the nearest  inferior  margin  1 0cm closest to the  superior  margin 2 1cm closest to the  posterior  margin  There is a blue dye infiltrating through the tissue and the mass  Continuous with the tumor at the medial end is a diffusely thickened  rubbery breast parenchyma    The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  The axillary nodes are sectioned into two big portions  the closest to the breast designated  proximal nodes   the other portion designated  distal nodes   Section code  B  superior margin and tumor C  inferior margin and tumor D E tumor F G rubbery area H N proximal nodes O S distal nodes Labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  lymph node  393 counts  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm firm  tan nodule  Sectioning reveals multiple white nodules separated by fatty tissue  Representative sections submitted in T U  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  BREAST  LEFT MEDIAL MARGIN  INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH FOCAL ATYPICALITIES  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  BREAST  MEDIAL MARGIN   PART B  LEBREAST WITH AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART C  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL   393    report_end  , Checked.
