s that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  previously cut into fragment of breast  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm ill defined  firm white lobulated area with focal cystic changes extending within 1 2cm of the medial surface  0 8cm of the anterior surface and 0 1cm of the posterior surface  The superior and lateral surfaces appear away from the lesion  The medial margin is frozen as frozen section  1  resubmitted in A  the inferior margin is frozen as frozen section  2  resubmitted in B  The anterior margin is frozen as frozen section  3 and resubmitted in C  The posterior margin is frozen as frozen section  4 and resubmitted in D  Two radial sections of anterior margin in E  inferoposterior sections in F through H  posterior surface radial section in I  and other sections in J and K  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 1  BREAST  MEDIAL MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 2  BREAST  INFERIOR MARGIN   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS PRESENT AT THE MARGIN  FOCALLY  SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 3  BREAST  ANTERIOR   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS PRESENT WITHIN CLOSE PROXIMITY OF INKED RESECTION MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 4  BREAST  POSTERIOR MARGIN   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE MARGIN  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  