Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 23 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with microcalcifications on left breast mammogram  and a strong family history of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  75    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 OF 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  25    COMEDO TYPE  MULTIFOCAL  MICROCALCIFICATIONS ARE PRESENT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 0 9cm in greatest diameter  Tumor focally extends to an inked resection margin  Tumor is identified in one small blood vessel  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with needle localization and accompanying roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a round  irregular  firm  white  gritty nodule  0 9cm in greatest extent  located at the distal portion of the wire and 0 8cm from the closest inked margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  now submitted in A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in B through J  with the nodule in E  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BRESAT   report_end  , Unchecked.
