l is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a soft tan probable lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a lumpectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  and is cut along the medial to lateral axis  Sectioning reveals an ill defined white tan relatively firm lesion that extends to 0 4cm of the superior margin  This lesion shows some extension into the surrounding unremarkable adipose tissue  This lesion measures approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Representative sections of the mass and nearest margin are submitted in cassettes B E  Representative sections of breast away from the mass are submitted in cassettes F G  Resident  JOSHUA B  KISH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL  EXCISION PART B  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 05 CLINICAL DATA  Fifty eight year old undergoing excision of left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    MUCINOUS  COLLOID  TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  PRESENT ADJACENT TO INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  un it number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast biopsy specimen with localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm tan firm well circumscribed nodule adherent to grossly unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  A representative section is frozen as FX  1  resubmitted as cassette J  The rest of the specimen entirely submitted in cassettes A through I with nodule in cassettes A through C  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   COLLOID CARCINOMA  O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
