and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm breast lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch designating superior margin  and a long stitch designating the lateral margin  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well defined tan firm nodule that comes to within 0 4cm of the posterior inked margin  1 7cm of the anterior margin  2 0cm of the superior margin  1 5cm of the inferior margin  1 5cm of the medial margin and 4 0cm of the lateral margin  The rest of the tissue is unremarkable  SECTION CODES  A  lateral margin  en face B  medial margin  en face C  superior margin D  nodule with posterior inferior margin E  anterior margin F  section medial to nodule with deep margin G  section lateral to nodule with deep margin HandI  representative section of the remaining tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal multiple tan pink lymph nodes  the largest measuring 3 5cm in greatest dimension  These are entirely submitted in AA through CC  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAS