rs that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 7 x 4 x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with guide wire and accompanying x ray showing focal calcifications  In this region is a firm white tan nodule visible at the surface  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  non compressible white tan nodule with irregular border that appears hemisected at the surface  A representative fragment of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  The remainder is submitted entirely in cassettes A through Z  with nodule in cassettes A through D  A representative section of the firm peripheral nodule is also saved frozen  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INVASIVE AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
