d by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 9cm portion of breast tissue with a long stitch designating the lateral margin and short stitch designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  black deep  blue superior  yellow inferior  orange anterior  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a firm  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm red  well circumscribed nodule with central white stellate scar and focal peripheral hemorrhage  The nodule comes to within the margins as follows  0 2cm from the deep  black  margin  0 2cm from the superior  blue  margin  0 8cm from the inferior  yellow  margin and 1 4cm from the anterior  orange  margin  A representative section of the nodule in relation to the deep  black  margin is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in A  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in B D  Representative sections away from the nodule are submitted E F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty breast tissue  There are stiches on the specimen with no designation as to orientation  The short stitch is now designated as superior and the long stitch is now designated as lateral  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  lateral orange  medial yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic biopsy site  The biopsy site comes to within 0 2cm of the closest  anterior  blue  margin  The biopsy site is surrounded by white yellow fibrous tissue  Sections are submitted as follows  G  Biopsy cavity with closest  anterior blue  margin H J  Representative sections of biopsy cavity K  Representative sections away from biopsy cavity Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  additional deep margin  is an unoriented piece of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  It is sectioned and submitted entirely in L M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  final shaved margin superior half of cavity  is an unoriented piece of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely N P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  final shaved margin inferior half of cavity  is an unoriented piece of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  It is sectioned and submitted entirely in Q R  Resident  SARAH ROLLINS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HEIKE VARNHOLT  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT DEEP   ADDITIONAL MARGIN PART C  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY  FINAL SHAVED PART D  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY   FINAL SHAVE PART E  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 12 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma with history of lumpectomy and axillary dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  2  PAGETOID SPREAD OF CARCINOMA INTO OVERLYING NIPPLE  PAGET S DISEASE   3  BIOPSY SITE WITH FAT NECROSIS AND GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE  SKIN OVERLYING PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE  EXCISION  FAT NECROSIS AND GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE  NOTE  The resection margins are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 04                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two parts  Labeled  left breast   is a 460 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm unoriented mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm overlying skin ellipse including 0 8cm in diameter nipple and unremarkable areolar  There is a 5 0cm scar on one border of the areolar  the specimen has not been oriented  The deep resection margin is a smooth fascial plane with small piece of skeletal muscle adherent  The entire specimen is somewhat  firm  with no localized mass and along one of the long borders of the skin is a biopsy cavity opened to the surface REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a breast mostly comprised of firm  fibrous tissue with small amounts of intervening yellow adipose tissue  The biopsy cavity measures 5 0cm in depth and contains a friable  hemorrhagic tissue  It is encapsulated by fibrous tissue and there is a small amount chalky yellow fat necrosis around the cavity  There is no gross evidence of tumor  The cavity extends 0 3cm from the deep resection margin  and is opened to the surface at one margin  both lateral margin are several centimeters away from the biopsy cavity  Labeled  skin overlying previous biopsy site   is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm piece of skin without apparent scars  remarkable only for surgical clamp marks  A small amount of subcutaneous tissue is adherent to the skin  including a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm smooth  fibrous  tan red area consistent with the roof of a biopsy cavity  Sectioning reveals a small amount of chalky light yellow fat necrosis between the roof of the biopsy cavity and the overlying skin  SECTION CODE  A  nipple and scar BandC  sections through the unroofed biopsy cavity area D  deep margin E G  biopsy cavity HandI  breast parenchyma JandK  sections through the skin overlying previous biopsy site  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART B  SKIN OVERLYING PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  NOTE  The tumor measures 0 9cm in greatest diameter  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  PAS and Grimelius stains show intracytoplasmic granules confirming the neuroendocrine nature of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm fragment of breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  stellate  centrally hemorrhagic  white tan lesion  0 9cm in greatest dimension  and 0 1cm from inked margin  No frozen is done  and the specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through H with  the lesion in cassettes C through E  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edward M Barksdale  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
